WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.200
If you want to hear the three hidden&nbsp;
reasons that Amanda Young defies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:06.960
Jigsaw near the end of her story, then&nbsp;
stick around to the end of this video.

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:15.360
One of Jigsaw’s goals with his victims was&nbsp;
to convert those who passed his tests into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:19.680
followers of his methods and one of his most&nbsp;
loyal followers was a woman named Amanda Young.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:23.280
Welcome to Horror History, my name is&nbsp;
Professor CZsWorld and in today’s lesson&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:26.960
I’ll be analysing the life of the&nbsp;
third major Jigsaw disciple, Amanda.

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:30.560
Out of everyone to help out Jigsaw over&nbsp;
the years, Amanda probably has the most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:34.320
troubled past, so let’s take it back to&nbsp;
her childhood to try to understand her.

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:42.080
While there is no canon explanation as&nbsp;
to why Amanda gets into a life of crime,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:46.480
there is cut content from Saw III that suggests&nbsp;
she was abused by her father, who used to lock&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:50.640
her up in the dark for hours on end. It’s&nbsp;
unlikely any future film will further explore&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:54.800
Amanda’s past, so that seems like a reasonable&nbsp;
explanation. I mean, I can live with that.

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:58.800
Her first canon appearance comes in the 1990s. She&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:02.320
was addicted to heroin and would often&nbsp;
shoot up while listening to The Used.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:12.000
That is their best album, so I guess not&nbsp;
all hope was lost on her, but others would not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:16.560
agree. She eventually attended a recovery clinic&nbsp;
called Homeward Bound, but her issues were so bad&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:20.880
that her doctor, Jill Tuck, considered her to&nbsp;
be a lost cause and dropped her from treatment.

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:24.640
It was during her time at Homeward Bound&nbsp;
that she first got on John Kramer’s radar,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:28.480
because he was married to Jill Tuck at the&nbsp;
time. It was also most likely where she met&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:32.720
another addict named Cecil Adams. One night, the&nbsp;
two planned to hold up the clinic after closing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:36.480
to steal some medication to relieve their&nbsp;
withdrawals. Even when Cecil had second&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:40.240
thoughts about committing the crime, Amada&nbsp;
convinced him to go back and carry it out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:44.880
and Cecil’s desperation eventually led to the&nbsp;
accidental miscarriage of Jill Tuck’s baby.

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:49.600
As far as we know, Jigsaw never knew Amanda&nbsp;
was involved with the incident, but police did.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:53.200
I’m guessing it has something to do with security&nbsp;
cameras at the clinic. Although she wasn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:57.440
technically guilty of anything in this instance,&nbsp;
one of the cops, Detective Eric Matthews saw to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.440 --> 00:02:01.440
it that she was punished by faking the evidence&nbsp;
needed to get her convicted of drug possession.

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:07.840
“You sent me to prison. I was&nbsp;
guilty of a lot of things,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:11.280
but not the drug charge you framed me for.”

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:15.200
She was eventually released, but did not realize&nbsp;
that the worst of her punishment was only just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:20.160
beginning. One day in May of 2004 she woke up&nbsp;
with the taste of blood and metal in her mouth.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:24.720
A contraption is bolted to her head, and videotape&nbsp;
starts playing and explains that it will open and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:29.280
rip her jaws apart if she’s unable to obtain&nbsp;
the key in 60 seconds. The key is located in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:33.120
the stomach of her cellmate, and she has to&nbsp;
do the unthinkable in order to obtain it.

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:37.360
She gets the key just in time, and she was&nbsp;
congratulated by the puppet from the tape.

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:40.000
“Congratulations. You are still alive.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:46.720
Most people are so ungrateful to be&nbsp;
alive. But not you. Not anymore.”

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:49.120
After escaping the building, she&nbsp;
goes straight to the police to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:51.600
report what happened to her, and&nbsp;
tells them that she is grateful,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:54.720
and that Jigsaw had helped her. When&nbsp;
she returned home after everything,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:59.040
John Kramer is sitting in her apartment, and&nbsp;
he tells her that her life has just begun.

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:03.200
That’s when she starts training with Jigsaw for&nbsp;
the next five months. One behaviour commonly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:06.480
seen in recovering addicts is feeding&nbsp;
their withdrawals with something else,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:09.760
and due to the fact that Amanda was coming&nbsp;
out of a chemical dependency on drugs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.760 --> 00:03:14.080
her brain had to find something else to latch&nbsp;
onto. This may explain why her loyalty to John,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:18.240
who was helping her overcome her problems by&nbsp;
teaching her his moral code, was so fierce.

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:22.000
She assisted him in putting together one of his&nbsp;
most complex games to date, which would take&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:27.200
place in October of 2004. She uses a pig mask to&nbsp;
disguise herself, a symbol that is perfect for her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:31.520
because the Year of the Pig in the Chinese zodiac&nbsp;
stands for rebirth, and Jigsaw believes she has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:35.200
been reborn as a better person.
 
JIGSAW: “The marks on your arms.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:38.880
They’re from another life.&nbsp;
You’ll leave that life behind.”

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:42.560
Jigsaw makes her promise her allegiance&nbsp;
before handing her an envelope containing a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:46.960
file on a photographer named Adam Stanheight. She&nbsp;
sneaks into Adam’s apartment and knocks him out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:51.440
using an injection. Then, she’s able to transport&nbsp;
his body to the site of the game using a dolly.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:55.760
Somehow, nobody sees this or finds it suspicious&nbsp;
in any way, and Amanda shackles his leg to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.760 --> 00:04:00.000
pipe, puts him in the bathtub and leaves the key&nbsp;
sitting on his chest. This was one of her first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:03.920
mistakes as John’s apprentice. Amanda was supposed&nbsp;
to place the key in a place where Adam had a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:08.000
chance to get it before it washed down the drain.&nbsp;
This would have made Adam’s game more winnable,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:12.160
but Amanda had a nasty habit of rigging&nbsp;
things against the participant of each game.

00:04:12.160 --> 00:04:15.680
I believe she does this because has become&nbsp;
so dependent on Jigsaw’s care for her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.680 --> 00:04:19.520
that she doesn’t like the idea of anyone&nbsp;
else surviving and becoming his disciple. She&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.520 --> 00:04:23.680
essentially wants to be the only one, so that she&nbsp;
can have all of John’s attention. We call this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:28.640
Jealous Girlfriend Syndrome. Rule number 1: NEVER&nbsp;
try to reason with someone who has this condition.

00:04:28.640 --> 00:04:31.600
After Jigsaw places himself at the&nbsp;
center of the game for surveillance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:34.960
Amanda puts on the final touches by turning&nbsp;
off the lights and closing the door.

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:38.640
Adam would end up losing the game, and his&nbsp;
punishment was to spend his remaining days in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.640 --> 00:04:43.440
bathroom, but the winner of the game, Dr. Gordon,&nbsp;
had promised to go back to save Adam, so Amanda,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.440 --> 00:04:47.440
not wanting there to be another survivor, sneaks&nbsp;
back into the bathroom to finish off Adam.

00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:50.560
Jigsaw would eventually discover her&nbsp;
transgression, but before he did,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:54.240
he believed that she was fully rehabilitated&nbsp;
by surviving the reverse bear trap,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:57.200
and brought her into Jill’s practice&nbsp;
as evidence that his methods can turn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.200 --> 00:05:00.400
a person’s life around in ways that&nbsp;
Jill’s medical treatments could not.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:04.640
Amanda was proud to have recovered from her&nbsp;
addiction even after Jill had given up on her.

00:05:04.640 --> 00:05:07.920
“It works. It’s real. He helped me.”

00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:11.440
However, at some point over the next year,&nbsp;
possibly due to the trauma of what she had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.440 --> 00:05:15.840
done to Adam, she began self-harming. Also&nbsp;
during this time she helps Jigsaw develop a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:19.440
new game with two major contributions.&nbsp;
First, she put together a test for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:23.200
man who had wrongfully imprisoned her, Eric&nbsp;
Matthews, in order to see if he could test&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:26.880
his restraint and solve the Jigsaw case&nbsp;
without resorting to dirty police work.

00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:30.320
Then, she was asked to take part&nbsp;
in the next game in October 2005,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.320 --> 00:05:34.080
which involved a group of ex-convicts who had&nbsp;
all been set up by Matthews, but were also all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.080 --> 00:05:38.320
guilty of other crimes. She would essentially play&nbsp;
the role that John had played in the first game,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.320 --> 00:05:42.160
by secretly placing herself in the center of&nbsp;
it so that she could ensure that all the rules&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.160 --> 00:05:46.000
are followed. If only she were still around, we&nbsp;
could give her a job with the Houston Astros.

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:49.520
The game challenged it’s participants to find&nbsp;
the antidotes hidden around the house as a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.520 --> 00:05:53.760
deadly nerve gas seeped into their systems. It&nbsp;
is likely that Amanda had already been treated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.760 --> 00:05:57.280
with the antidote before ever going into the&nbsp;
game, because she had already passed her test,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.280 --> 00:06:00.480
and would need to stay healthy in&nbsp;
order to facilitate the game. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.480 --> 00:06:04.240
it was possible she was partially being&nbsp;
tested again, because she had once more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.240 --> 00:06:07.840
demonstrated her inability to cherish&nbsp;
life when she started cutting herself.

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:10.640
I personally think she was given an&nbsp;
antidote, because she doesn’t show&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:14.000
the same symptoms of the nerve gas as&nbsp;
the others, but Jigsaw was still making&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:17.760
her repent for her self-harm just by putting&nbsp;
her in a dangerous situation with a bunch of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.760 --> 00:06:21.440
ex-convicts. She also doesn’t seem to know&nbsp;
all the secrets of the house, for example,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:25.040
she is surprised to find that the trap&nbsp;
door under the safe is locked later on.

00:06:25.040 --> 00:06:28.880
But despite her theoretically being in less&nbsp;
danger than the others, Amanda would endure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.880 --> 00:06:33.840
more suffering than ever before when the Nerve&nbsp;
Gas House game didn’t quite go according to plan…

00:06:41.520 --> 00:06:45.760
When the Nerve Gas House game begins, Amanda&nbsp;
acts as if she's in a panic to help sell the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.760 --> 00:06:50.000
idea that she's a participant. Yeah, Amanda&nbsp;
is a pretty decent actress, unlike Adam.

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:51.840
*Adam pretending to choke (poorly)*

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:54.160
Amanda uncovers the tape with the instructions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.160 --> 00:06:57.600
for the game and explains her past&nbsp;
experience being in a Jigsaw trap.

00:06:57.600 --> 00:07:00.080
"He's testing us. He wants us to survive this."

00:07:00.080 --> 00:07:02.000
The first death occurs when a man named Gus&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:05.520
ignores Jigsaw's advice not to use a key&nbsp;
on the door. The others escape the room&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:08.240
and begin searching the house&nbsp;
and Amanda turns on the lights.

00:07:08.240 --> 00:07:11.440
The next death occurs when a man named&nbsp;
Obi fails to retrieve the antidotes from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.440 --> 00:07:15.200
his trap inside of the furnace. When one&nbsp;
of the participants, a boy named Daniel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.200 --> 00:07:18.720
asks why Amanda was chosen for the game, she&nbsp;
tells him that it was because she was a junkie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.720 --> 00:07:22.160
which is a clue about one of the things they&nbsp;
are supposed to be figuring out: which is that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.160 --> 00:07:26.400
each of them were framed by the kid's father:&nbsp;
Eric Matthews. She also explains that she was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.400 --> 00:07:30.640
included in this second game because she took&nbsp;
up self-harm as an unhealthy coping mechanism.

00:07:30.640 --> 00:07:33.920
They find the next trap, which is&nbsp;
intended for Xavier, a drug dealer.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.920 --> 00:07:37.120
His test is to metaphorically crawl&nbsp;
through the same pit that the junkies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.120 --> 00:07:40.960
he dealt to did, by finding the key to&nbsp;
the antidote in a huge pile of needles.

00:07:40.960 --> 00:07:45.040
However, Xavier abuses his position as&nbsp;
the biggest guy in the room and forces&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:45.040 --> 00:07:48.400
Amanda to do his test for him. He&nbsp;
tosses her into the needle pit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:52.560
which is one of the most horrifying twists that&nbsp;
could have possibly gone down for her character.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.560 --> 00:07:57.200
Amanda had already been through so much suffering&nbsp;
in order to overcome her addiction, and now she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.200 --> 00:08:02.080
was being thrown back into it, literally thrown&nbsp;
back into a world of needles and desperation.

00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:05.920
There's also the risk for Amanda to go through&nbsp;
a relapse, which is when a drug user or someone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.920 --> 00:08:10.000
suffering from an addiction slips up once and&nbsp;
returns to the negative behaviours because of it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:14.080
And that can be a very dangerous thing, because&nbsp;
after being off of the heroin for a while,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:14.080 --> 00:08:17.520
her tolerance is likely to change&nbsp;
and put her at risk for an overdose.

00:08:17.520 --> 00:08:20.960
We don't know what was in the syringes&nbsp;
in the needle pit, but for those reasons,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.960 --> 00:08:24.480
and the fact that many people are already&nbsp;
afraid of needles, this is widely regarded&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:27.680
as the most uncomfortable trap&nbsp;
in the entire Saw franchise.

00:08:27.680 --> 00:08:30.240
At least it wasn't a pit filled&nbsp;
with various LEGO pieces though.

00:08:30.240 --> 00:08:33.280
COMMERCIAL: "A man-da has fallen into the river, in LEGO City!"

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:37.920
This was absolutely traumatizing for Amanda,&nbsp;
and this is just speculation, but I'd point to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.920 --> 00:08:42.400
this as the reason she becomes so unforgiving&nbsp;
towards victims of the traps from here on out.

00:08:42.400 --> 00:08:47.120
She finds the key with 7 seconds to go, but that's&nbsp;
not enough time for Xavier to unlock the door with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:47.120 --> 00:08:51.680
the antidote. I think the fact still remains that&nbsp;
he was nearly able to escape without suffering or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:51.680 --> 00:08:56.240
rehabilitating at all, and this stuck with Amanda&nbsp;
for the rest of her time working for Jigsaw.

00:08:56.240 --> 00:08:58.720
Soon after, the group splits up&nbsp;
to continue searching for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:58.720 --> 00:09:02.240
antidotes and the clue about Daniel's&nbsp;
link to Eric Matthews is discovered.

00:09:02.240 --> 00:09:04.960
“What are you doing with&nbsp;
him? This is your father?”

00:09:04.960 --> 00:09:08.960
So the question that I have here is: did&nbsp;
Amanda know that Daniel was Eric’s son?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.960 --> 00:09:12.160
We’ve already seen that she has the ability&nbsp;
to act, when she pretends to be surprised&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.160 --> 00:09:16.240
that she is back inside of Jigsaw’s game,&nbsp;
but was she acting when she said this line?

00:09:16.240 --> 00:09:18.080
“Tell me that’s not your father.”

00:09:18.080 --> 00:09:22.800
I think she is, and here’s why. First: the fact&nbsp;
that she created the test for Eric Matthews.

00:09:22.800 --> 00:09:24.000
“Hello Eric.”

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:27.600
She likely would have known a lot about him&nbsp;
in order to do this, and at the very least,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.600 --> 00:09:30.640
read his profile and known&nbsp;
his most basic family info.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:30.640 --> 00:09:35.280
I also think her reaction when Daniel almost&nbsp;
voluntarily reveals who his father is early on,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:35.280 --> 00:09:38.080
tells us that Amanda knew all&nbsp;
along. Let’s roll that clip.

00:09:40.468 --> 00:09:44.240
DANIEL: "I mean, I've been in trouble a few times, you know? In and out of stuff.

00:09:44.240 --> 00:09:50.800
My Dad’s a… he’s um… he’s a real hard&nbsp;
ass. He’s probably got half the city&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.800 --> 00:09:55.240
right now looking for me just so he can&nbsp;
kick my ass for disappearing on him.”

00:09:56.080 --> 00:09:57.600
AMANDA: “Yeah. Probably.”

00:09:57.600 --> 00:10:01.840
She seems kind of panicked when he’s about to&nbsp;
out himself, and then relieved when he doesn’t.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.840 --> 00:10:05.760
We don’t get to see much of her reaction when the&nbsp;
truth is revealed though, because moments later,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.760 --> 00:10:10.160
one of the other contestants chokes on the nerve&nbsp;
gas and passes away in Amanda’s arms. There’s no&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.160 --> 00:10:14.400
time to mourn however, because Xavier can be heard&nbsp;
calling after her in the distance. She surveys&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:14.400 --> 00:10:18.560
the house and discovers that he’s already taken&nbsp;
care of Jonas and will likely be after her life&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.560 --> 00:10:22.960
next. She grabs Daniel and takes him to the first&nbsp;
room where they barricade themselves for safety.

00:10:22.960 --> 00:10:26.960
Together, they’re able to move the safe and&nbsp;
uncover a trap door leading down to the basement&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:26.960 --> 00:10:31.040
just before Xavier knocks the door down. The&nbsp;
basement is a series of tunnels and rooms,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:31.040 --> 00:10:34.160
one of which is the bathroom where&nbsp;
she had brought Adam one year earlier.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.160 --> 00:10:36.480
She leads Daniel there, with Xavier close behind.

00:10:36.480 --> 00:10:40.720
The two devise a plan that has been used time&nbsp;
and time again in the Saw series, pretending to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:40.720 --> 00:10:45.520
be dead, which is ultimately how Daniel gains the&nbsp;
upper hand on Xavier. Once again, Amanda’s acting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:45.520 --> 00:10:49.840
skills shine right here, probably one of the under&nbsp;
appreciated strengths of her character. With them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.840 --> 00:10:54.080
being the only two survivors, she gets Daniel&nbsp;
the antidote out of the safe and saves his life.

00:10:54.080 --> 00:10:57.520
He’s still very weak, and when the doors&nbsp;
open after the three hours has expired,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:57.520 --> 00:11:01.520
she takes him to Jigsaw, where he’s given&nbsp;
an oxygen mask and safely stowed in another&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:01.520 --> 00:11:05.520
safe in Jigsaw’s workshop. But before&nbsp;
this game was over, Amanda had one more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:05.520 --> 00:11:10.797
job that would put her face to face with&nbsp;
the man who wronged her so many years ago.

00:11:19.280 --> 00:11:23.760
Amanda later returned to the Nerve Gas house,&nbsp;
once again disguised in robes and pig mask in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:23.760 --> 00:11:28.320
order to carry out the final part of the test for&nbsp;
Eric Matthews in case he failed his test. He would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:28.320 --> 00:11:32.960
fail by using police brutality to force John&nbsp;
to take him to the location of the game. Amanda&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:32.960 --> 00:11:36.880
waited for him in the bathroom, and injected&nbsp;
him with the anesthetic before he could react.

00:11:36.880 --> 00:11:40.800
She shackled him to the pipe where she had once&nbsp;
shackled Adam and leaves behind a tape, which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:45.200
explains that this was her training, and she would&nbsp;
eventually be the one to carry on John's work.

00:11:45.200 --> 00:11:49.280
She leaves him in the bathroom echoing&nbsp;
Jigsaw's signature phrase "Game Over",&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:49.280 --> 00:11:53.600
thinking he'll probably die there, but to her&nbsp;
surprise, she finds that he's able to escape by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:53.600 --> 00:11:58.080
crushing his foot and sliding out the shackle.&nbsp;
She hides when she realizes he's on the loose,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:58.080 --> 00:12:00.800
but he manages to catch her&nbsp;
before she leaves the house.

00:12:00.800 --> 00:12:04.400
The two get into a skirmish in which&nbsp;
she immobilizes him even further by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:04.400 --> 00:12:07.520
attacking his weak ankle. At first&nbsp;
she's willing to leave it at that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:07.520 --> 00:12:11.120
but when she hears what he yells out&nbsp;
after her, she stops in her tracks.

00:12:13.323 --> 00:12:18.880
"You're not Jigsaw! You hear me? You're nothing!"

00:12:18.880 --> 00:12:23.440
Remember, Amanda had nothing after coming out&nbsp;
of her life as an addict and latched onto John,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:23.440 --> 00:12:26.320
so her training to become&nbsp;
Jigsaw meant everything to her.

00:12:26.320 --> 00:12:30.800
Hearing those words, "you're not Jigsaw", hurt&nbsp;
her more than anything else possibly could have.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:30.800 --> 00:12:35.520
She literally falls to her knees at this remark,&nbsp;
and that's when she decides that she will not let&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:35.520 --> 00:12:39.920
Eric Matthews live and goes back to finish him&nbsp;
off. She’s also starting to believe that not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:39.920 --> 00:12:44.000
everyone who survives a trap experiences the&nbsp;
same rehabilitation that she did, and I think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:44.000 --> 00:12:48.320
she realizes that Matthews hasn’t changed after&nbsp;
making it out of his shackle in the bathroom.

00:12:48.320 --> 00:12:51.920
The movies don't actually show what she did&nbsp;
to him, but we can assume it's pretty bad,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:51.920 --> 00:12:55.680
because Amanda actually believes that&nbsp;
Matthews is dead for the next 6 months. 
 &nbsp;

00:12:55.680 --> 00:12:58.480
During this time, she continues&nbsp;
her apprenticeship with Jigsaw,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:58.480 --> 00:13:02.160
but he begins to fear that she's not fit for&nbsp;
the job after seeing her emotions get the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:02.160 --> 00:13:05.840
better of her a couple times now, first&nbsp;
against Adam and now against Matthews.

00:13:05.840 --> 00:13:07.840
Jigsaw devises a new test for Amanda,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:07.840 --> 00:13:11.760
to test her self control and see if she's&nbsp;
really capable of bearing the Jigsaw name,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:11.760 --> 00:13:16.480
or if Matthews was right, and Amanda Young was&nbsp;
not destined to take over the role of Jigsaw.

00:13:16.480 --> 00:13:20.000
Amanda is asked to help prepare for this&nbsp;
game, because she doesn't know she's being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:20.000 --> 00:13:23.440
tested along with the other participants.&nbsp;
I'm sure all of us can relate to finding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:23.440 --> 00:13:28.080
out about a test on the day of. Not&nbsp;
a good feeling. Not a good feeling.

00:13:28.080 --> 00:13:31.920
Also helping to put together the next game&nbsp;
is another Jigsaw disciple, Mark Hoffman.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:31.920 --> 00:13:35.760
Amanda and Hoffman develop a rivalry, they&nbsp;
both want to be the one to take over John's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:35.760 --> 00:13:39.520
work after his passing, but neither wants&nbsp;
to share that honor with the other person.

00:13:39.520 --> 00:13:43.360
She also develops an even closer bond with&nbsp;
John, who is getting physically weaker by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:43.360 --> 00:13:47.520
the day because of his cancer and requires Amanda&nbsp;
to push him around in a wheelchair and basically&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:47.520 --> 00:13:51.920
be his personal caretaker. She begins living in&nbsp;
a small room at the Gideon Meat Packing Plant,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:51.920 --> 00:13:54.880
which would be Jigsaw’s new base&nbsp;
of operations from here on out.

00:13:54.880 --> 00:13:58.400
She would also take on the responsibility&nbsp;
of setting up John's games, since he was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:58.400 --> 00:14:03.120
no longer able to do much physically. However,&nbsp;
Amanda, still shaken by what she had endured&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:03.120 --> 00:14:06.720
at the Nerve Gas House, was not in the&nbsp;
mindset of giving people a second chance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:06.720 --> 00:14:10.640
which is the whole point of Jigsaw's games,&nbsp;
to give people the chance to rehabilitate.

00:14:10.640 --> 00:14:13.840
She instead started to see them&nbsp;
as vigilante acts of punishment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:13.840 --> 00:14:17.440
and made her contraptions into&nbsp;
unwinnable death traps rather than games.

00:14:17.440 --> 00:14:21.600
Her first victim was a man named Troy, who was&nbsp;
a fellow patient of Homeward Bound Clinic. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:21.600 --> 00:14:25.280
was placed in a classroom, and yes, you&nbsp;
can see I took some inspiration for my&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:25.280 --> 00:14:28.320
decorations here in the Horror History&nbsp;
classroom, I should've spent less time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:28.320 --> 00:14:32.720
praising Amanda for her ability to act and given&nbsp;
more compliments on her interior design skills.

00:14:32.720 --> 00:14:35.120
But yeah, she put these chains&nbsp;
into Troy's flesh and made him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:35.120 --> 00:14:38.240
yank them out of his body in order&nbsp;
to escape. There was also a timer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:38.240 --> 00:14:41.680
and this nailbomb would go off and kill him&nbsp;
if he was still in the room when it expired.

00:14:41.680 --> 00:14:44.320
Only problem was that the door was welded shut,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:44.320 --> 00:14:47.760
so Troy never even had the chance&nbsp;
regardless of the outcome of the game.

00:14:47.760 --> 00:14:51.600
There was also a game for one of the police&nbsp;
detectives, a woman named Alison Kerry. She&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:51.600 --> 00:14:55.280
was tasked with reaching into a beaker of&nbsp;
acid to retrieve the key to her trap, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:55.280 --> 00:14:59.680
Amanda had rigged this game as well, putting in&nbsp;
the wrong key, resulting in the death of Alison.

00:14:59.680 --> 00:15:04.160
In her spare time, Amanda practices her mechanical&nbsp;
engineering skills and builds a collar device that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:04.160 --> 00:15:08.080
would be used in the next game. But at some&nbsp;
point, the pressure of her training to become&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:08.080 --> 00:15:12.240
the next Jigsaw successor and the guilt about&nbsp;
all of the horrible things she had done to her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:12.240 --> 00:15:17.040
victims caused her to have a relapse. Not a&nbsp;
drug relapse, but self-mutilation relapse.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:17.040 --> 00:15:21.200
After promising Jigsaw to leave that behaviour&nbsp;
in her past life, she knew she had to keep it a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:21.200 --> 00:15:25.200
secret, and did so by cutting her inner thighs&nbsp;
and wearing jeans every day to cover it up.

00:15:25.200 --> 00:15:29.600
One day in April of 2006, during one of the&nbsp;
final preparation days for this next game,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:29.600 --> 00:15:34.160
Amanda gets into a little quarrel with Hoffman.&nbsp;
She mockingly asks him when his test will be, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:34.160 --> 00:15:38.400
he tells her he doesn’t need to be tested, because&nbsp;
he did not take his life for granted as she did.

00:15:38.400 --> 00:15:40.560
Amanda boasts that he might&nbsp;
as well get used to her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:40.560 --> 00:15:43.840
because she’s not going anywhere,&nbsp;
but Hoffman doesn’t seem so sure.

00:15:43.840 --> 00:15:45.280
“You sure about that?”

00:15:45.280 --> 00:15:48.480
John tells Amanda that it’s time to&nbsp;
get Dr. Lynn Denlon from the hospital,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:48.480 --> 00:15:52.720
which means the next game is about to begin.&nbsp;
Amanda shows up to Angel of Mercy Hospital and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:52.720 --> 00:15:57.120
waits until Dr. Denlon is alone in the changing&nbsp;
room. She locks her in, then attacks her and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:57.120 --> 00:16:00.800
uses a wheelchair to transport her back to&nbsp;
the building where John is being kept. When&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:00.800 --> 00:16:05.120
Lynn wakes up, Amanda brings her into the room&nbsp;
with John, who explains the rules of the game.

00:16:05.120 --> 00:16:09.360
Dr. Denlon’s collar is linked to John’s heart&nbsp;
rate monitor, so if he dies, or she moves out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:09.360 --> 00:16:13.200
of range by leaving the building, the collar&nbsp;
will explode and kill her. Her goal was to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:13.200 --> 00:16:17.440
keep John alive until Lynn’s husband, Jeff&nbsp;
Denlon, finished his trial in another area,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:17.440 --> 00:16:21.040
but Amanda and Lynn did not know that&nbsp;
Jeff was the other person being tested.

00:16:21.040 --> 00:16:25.760
By doing this, John was also able to test Amanda.&nbsp;
John was aware that Amanda had rigged many of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:25.760 --> 00:16:30.400
her tests into execution devices, so he was&nbsp;
testing her ability to let Lynn Denlon’s test&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:30.400 --> 00:16:34.720
go uninterrupted. If Amanda were to interfere&nbsp;
and do something that resulted in Lynn’s death,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:34.720 --> 00:16:38.080
then Jeff would likely come through and&nbsp;
get revenge on Amanda. So this was just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:38.080 --> 00:16:41.840
as much Amanda’s game as it was Lynn’s&nbsp;
or Jeff’s. She had to learn to control&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:41.840 --> 00:16:46.080
her emotions and let the game play out, but&nbsp;
Dr. Denlon would not make that easy for her.

00:16:46.080 --> 00:16:48.240
Hoffman delivers Jeff to&nbsp;
the beginning of his game,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:48.240 --> 00:16:53.120
and Amanda would keep tabs via computer monitors&nbsp;
and periodically update John on his progress.

00:16:53.120 --> 00:16:57.120
After examining him, Dr. Denlon’s suggestion&nbsp;
is that they take John to a hospital because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:57.120 --> 00:17:00.240
his brain was herniating. This&nbsp;
suggestion quickly angers Amanda,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:00.240 --> 00:17:04.000
she’s already letting her emotional nature get&nbsp;
the better of her. She tells Lynn that a hospital&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:04.000 --> 00:17:07.920
is pretty much out of the question. Amanda&nbsp;
is so ill-mannered and physically threatening&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:07.920 --> 00:17:11.840
when speaking to Lynn, that the dying John&nbsp;
Kramer actually feels the need to intervene.

00:17:11.840 --> 00:17:16.320
“Amanda! The doctor can’t do&nbsp;
what’s being asked of her if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:16.320 --> 00:17:20.080
you’re threatening her. The rules of&nbsp;
our game have been made very clear.”

00:17:20.080 --> 00:17:24.480
Each game has a rule-keeper. It’s John in the&nbsp;
bathroom game, Amanda in the Nerve Gas House&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:24.480 --> 00:17:28.560
and John again here in the Death Collar Game,&nbsp;
but that would go out the window when John goes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:28.560 --> 00:17:33.280
into some kind of life-threatening seizure episode&nbsp;
that would force Lynn and Amanda to work together.

00:17:41.040 --> 00:17:44.160
John loses control of his body&nbsp;
and thrashes around violently,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:44.160 --> 00:17:47.440
to the point that Dr. Denlon is unable&nbsp;
to restrain him enough to help him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:47.440 --> 00:17:52.400
She calls for Amanda to help hold him down and&nbsp;
administer oxygen. Eventually, he stabilizes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:52.400 --> 00:17:56.080
but the scare hits Amanda hard, and she has&nbsp;
to leave the room with tears in her eyes.

00:17:56.080 --> 00:18:00.240
We’ve already established that Amanda’s emotions&nbsp;
are her weakness, and I think seeing her idol,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:00.240 --> 00:18:03.840
Jigsaw, she man she views as her&nbsp;
saviour, in such vulnerable state&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:03.840 --> 00:18:07.360
brought down her psyche even further,&nbsp;
and all of the experiences she would go&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:07.360 --> 00:18:10.640
through that day would push her closer&nbsp;
and closer to the edge of a breakdown.

00:18:10.640 --> 00:18:14.960
Even after that though, Amanda still insists they&nbsp;
must perform the operation at the meatpacking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:14.960 --> 00:18:19.120
plant, rather than moving to a hospital&nbsp;
and… you know… getting them all arrested.

00:18:19.120 --> 00:18:23.120
Lynn reluctantly agrees and gives Amanda&nbsp;
a list of materials needed which includes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:23.120 --> 00:18:27.440
an anaesthetic and a power drill. I can only&nbsp;
imagine how awkward it was at the checkout line.

00:18:27.440 --> 00:18:31.200
When she gets back from getting the supplies,&nbsp;
she discovers Lynn taking a peak at the traps&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:31.200 --> 00:18:34.880
and weapons stored in the area outside the&nbsp;
operating room and mockingly challenges her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:34.880 --> 00:18:38.080
to try to do her best Jack Torrance&nbsp;
on her, explaining that if she does,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:38.080 --> 00:18:44.080
John could easily rip off the heart rate monitor&nbsp;
and turn Dr. Denlon into Dr. Pile of Ashes.

00:18:44.080 --> 00:18:48.320
Lynn is still not confident that these makeshift&nbsp;
tools will get the job done, and Amanda tells her,

00:18:48.320 --> 00:18:50.880
“You’d be surprised what tools could save a life.”

00:18:50.880 --> 00:18:55.200
...which is one of Amanda's most intelligent lines&nbsp;
because of its double meaning. She's giving Lynn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:55.200 --> 00:18:59.200
the tools she'll need to help John, but also&nbsp;
talking about how the tools in front of them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:59.200 --> 00:19:03.760
the traps, helped to save her life by making&nbsp;
her appreciate life again and get off of drugs.

00:19:03.760 --> 00:19:07.360
Before the surgery, Amanda checks back&nbsp;
in on Jeff's progress and updates John&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:07.360 --> 00:19:09.840
on his whereabouts. He had just&nbsp;
made it through the first room,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:09.840 --> 00:19:13.440
and Amanda would soon face the first&nbsp;
obstacle in her portion of the game as well.

00:19:13.440 --> 00:19:17.440
He asks her to retrieve an envelope with her&nbsp;
name on it in his desk drawer in the other room.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:17.440 --> 00:19:21.520
Since John had about as much energy as a horror&nbsp;
YouTuber the day after Halloween at this point, he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:21.520 --> 00:19:25.520
had Hoffman place the letter there. We never find&nbsp;
out what the original letter was supposed to say&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:25.520 --> 00:19:29.520
though, because Hoffman pulls the old switcheroo&nbsp;
and leaves his own letter in the envelope.

00:19:29.520 --> 00:19:33.680
Before going to retrieve it, the brain surgery&nbsp;
takes place and Amanda fills the role of Lynn’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:33.680 --> 00:19:38.000
medical assistant, during which she’s unable to&nbsp;
cope with the seriousness of the situation and has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:38.000 --> 00:19:42.400
to look away for most of it. At the end of the&nbsp;
operation, John slipped into a critical state,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:42.400 --> 00:19:47.040
causing his heart rate to plummet and his brain to&nbsp;
fire off a random memory of him and his then-wife.

00:19:47.040 --> 00:19:50.240
When his heart rate stabilized, he was&nbsp;
still in the hallucination of his wife&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:50.240 --> 00:19:52.880
causing him to touch Lynn’s&nbsp;
elbow and say, “I love you.”

00:19:52.880 --> 00:19:54.960
And that caused Amanda to do this.

00:19:54.960 --> 00:19:57.840
🎵 Intense Horror Music 🎵

00:19:57.840 --> 00:20:00.960
Amanda storms off to her bed, but&nbsp;
instead of playing with her creepy doll,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:00.960 --> 00:20:06.080
she opens up a secret box full of sharp objects.&nbsp;
Ohhhh, maybe that’s why she got into The Used.

00:20:06.080 --> 00:20:12.720
“Found a box of sharp objects,&nbsp;
what a beautiful THING!!”

00:20:12.720 --> 00:20:15.680
She cuts herself again to distract&nbsp;
herself from the emotional pain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:15.680 --> 00:20:19.280
she was going through and bandages up the&nbsp;
wounds to keep them a secret from Jigsaw.

00:20:19.280 --> 00:20:22.560
When she comes back into the room&nbsp;
she’s in full jealous girlfriend mode,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:22.560 --> 00:20:27.600
and despite the 15 year age difference, she starts&nbsp;
weirdly kissing his neck…? I don’t speak woman,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:27.600 --> 00:20:31.280
but my guess is that his was her way&nbsp;
of telling Lynn, “back off b****!”

00:20:31.280 --> 00:20:35.600
Lynn tells Amanda that he can’t hear her, so&nbsp;
Amanda freaks out and pulls a gun on Lynn.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:35.600 --> 00:20:39.040
It turns out that Jigsaw is actually&nbsp;
awake, and he tells off Amanda and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:39.040 --> 00:20:42.720
asks to be left alone with Lynn, which&nbsp;
was probably another phase of the test.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:42.720 --> 00:20:46.000
John knew that this would make Amanda&nbsp;
jealous, but he needed to push her to her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:46.000 --> 00:20:50.000
limit in order to determine if she’d really be&nbsp;
capable of handling her emotions going forward.

00:20:50.000 --> 00:20:53.920
To further this, the next time Amanda comes&nbsp;
into the room, Jigsaw tells her they’re fine,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:53.920 --> 00:20:57.760
they don’t need her, which sends her&nbsp;
into an even darker rage. But John knew&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:57.760 --> 00:21:01.440
that in order for Amanda to take over for&nbsp;
him, she would have to be self-motivated,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:01.440 --> 00:21:04.400
and that means not just acting out&nbsp;
of her love for John. In other words,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:04.400 --> 00:21:08.400
she had to become less emotionally dependent&nbsp;
on him, and the only way to do that is to let&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:08.400 --> 00:21:11.840
go of that connection that was established&nbsp;
when he saved her from her life of drugs. If&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:11.840 --> 00:21:15.440
she could contain her jealousy, John would&nbsp;
be convinced that she’d passed the test.

00:21:15.440 --> 00:21:19.440
But he wasn’t counting on what would happen&nbsp;
next: Amanda went to go find the envelope&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:19.440 --> 00:21:23.440
from John that Hoffman had interfered&nbsp;
with. She reads the note, which says:

00:21:23.440 --> 00:21:31.040
“Amanda - You were with Cecil the night Jill&nbsp;
lost Gideon. You killed their child. You know&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:31.040 --> 00:21:39.360
it and I know it, so do exactly as I say. Kill&nbsp;
Lynn Denlon or I will tell John what you did.”

00:21:40.480 --> 00:21:45.200
Hoffman knew about this mistake that Amanda had&nbsp;
made back in the 90s, but he also knew how Amanda&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:45.200 --> 00:21:49.600
felt about John. She would be heartbroken if John&nbsp;
found out that she was involved in the death of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:49.600 --> 00:21:54.160
his child, so she has to seriously consider&nbsp;
caving into Hoffman’s demand and killing Lynn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:54.160 --> 00:21:58.720
Denlon. She already disliked Dr. Denlon because&nbsp;
of her perceived relationship with John, but this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:58.720 --> 00:22:03.120
note from Hoffman motivated her even further, and&nbsp;
might just be enough to push her over the edge.

00:22:03.120 --> 00:22:06.640
However, Amanda Young would not go down&nbsp;
without a fight, and she would find a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:06.640 --> 00:22:11.840
clever way to get back at Hoffman, before the&nbsp;
grand culmination of the Death Collar Game.

00:22:16.800 --> 00:22:21.200
After being blackmailed by Detective Hoffman,&nbsp;
Amanda secretly made a very important move to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:21.200 --> 00:22:25.760
get revenge on him. In a flurry of emotions, she&nbsp;
goes to the cell where Jeff and Lynn’s daughter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:25.760 --> 00:22:29.920
Corbett Denlon is being kept. Corbett has been&nbsp;
placed there by Hoffman, on John’s orders,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:29.920 --> 00:22:33.920
as an extra incentive for Jeff to make the&nbsp;
right choice after escaping from his game.

00:22:33.920 --> 00:22:36.960
Remember, Amanda doesn’t know&nbsp;
that Jeff and Lynn are married,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:36.960 --> 00:22:40.720
so she probably doesn’t realize that Corbett&nbsp;
is Lynn’s daughter. She’s probably just knows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:40.720 --> 00:22:44.160
Corbett as Jeff’s daughter. But she&nbsp;
does know that Hoffman may very well&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:44.160 --> 00:22:47.920
be the sole survivor by the end of the&nbsp;
day, and tells Corbett the following:

00:22:47.920 --> 00:22:51.760
“Don’t trust the one who saves you.”

00:22:51.760 --> 00:22:55.840
Just remember that, because I’ll come back to&nbsp;
it shortly. Not long after, Jeff completes his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:55.840 --> 00:22:59.760
final test, and he’s basically about to be on&nbsp;
his way to the operation room. Since Lynn was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:59.760 --> 00:23:04.720
able to keep John alive for all of it, he says&nbsp;
she is free to go, but Amanda has other ideas.

00:23:04.720 --> 00:23:08.240
She decided that her best move given the&nbsp;
circumstances is to give in to Hoffman’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:08.240 --> 00:23:11.600
demands and take out Lynn, and after doing&nbsp;
so. John commands her to unlock Lynn’s collar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:11.600 --> 00:23:15.600
and let her go, but she defies him. Her&nbsp;
emotional state has spiraled into such a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:15.600 --> 00:23:19.280
frenzy that I think Amanda actually starts&nbsp;
to believe that she knows better than John.

00:23:19.280 --> 00:23:22.800
I imagine that her line of logic is that&nbsp;
John would be more hurt by discovering&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:22.800 --> 00:23:26.880
that Amanda was involved in Gideon’s death&nbsp;
than he would be by Amanda disobeying him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:26.880 --> 00:23:30.560
She also really doesn’t like Lynn,&nbsp;
so this is the easy choice to make.

00:23:30.560 --> 00:23:33.280
John tries to convince her that&nbsp;
her own life is in Lynn’s hands,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:33.280 --> 00:23:36.160
but that just ends up upsetting Amanda&nbsp;
even more. Remember, rule number 1 of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:36.160 --> 00:23:39.280
Jealous Girlfriend Syndrome is to&nbsp;
NEVER try to reason with the person.

00:23:39.280 --> 00:23:42.240
John brings up the victims he left&nbsp;
alive that Amanda tried to kill,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:42.240 --> 00:23:46.160
like Adam and Detective Matthews, but Amanda&nbsp;
claims that those people deserved to die,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:46.160 --> 00:23:49.520
and what she did was not different than&nbsp;
what Jigsaw does. She believes that Dr.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:49.520 --> 00:23:54.160
Denlon should not go free because she had not&nbsp;
rehabilitated, and through her eyes, nobody had.

00:23:54.160 --> 00:23:58.640
There are obviously two factors at play here,&nbsp;
Amanda’s beliefs and Hoffman’s blackmail. I do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:58.640 --> 00:24:02.480
think that Amanda genuinely has doubts that&nbsp;
John’s methods work. As I mentioned earlier,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:02.480 --> 00:24:05.440
she had experienced first hand how&nbsp;
someone like Xavier could get through&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:05.440 --> 00:24:08.880
his test without rehabilitating, and she&nbsp;
sees it again when Detective Matthews&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:08.880 --> 00:24:12.400
makes a huge sacrifice to escape from the&nbsp;
bathroom, but still tries to get revenge&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:12.400 --> 00:24:15.920
on Amanda and doesn’t seem to have changed.&nbsp;
Not to mention the fact that she eventually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:15.920 --> 00:24:19.200
relapsed and started cutting herself&nbsp;
again, even under Jigsaw’s training.

00:24:19.200 --> 00:24:21.600
Hoffman’s letter was really&nbsp;
just kind of an extra incentive.

00:24:21.600 --> 00:24:25.840
So Amanda shoots Lynn, and shortly after, Jeff&nbsp;
comes and sees that his wife has been killed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:25.840 --> 00:24:28.800
and shoots Amanda. In her final&nbsp;
moments, John reaches out to her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:28.800 --> 00:24:32.080
and explains that this was her test.&nbsp;
When John had said he was testing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:32.080 --> 00:24:36.000
“your will to live and keep someone alive,”&nbsp;
he was talking to Amanda, not Lynn.

00:24:36.000 --> 00:24:40.160
He knew that she was making her games unwinnable,&nbsp;
but since his remaining days were very limited,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:40.160 --> 00:24:43.840
he decided to give her one last chance&nbsp;
out of desperation and she had failed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:43.840 --> 00:24:49.120
him. So Amanda passes away, a victim of&nbsp;
her own actions, on April 28th, 2006.

00:24:49.120 --> 00:24:52.240
Despite the fact that she had failed her&nbsp;
test, and would be unable to take over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:52.240 --> 00:24:56.880
for John after his passing, she was still able&nbsp;
to help him in one small way after his death.

00:24:56.880 --> 00:25:00.800
John would only survive a couple minutes longer&nbsp;
than Amanda, and that left Mark Hoffman as the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:00.800 --> 00:25:04.880
man who would take over Jigsaw’s legacy and&nbsp;
carry out the rest of his requests. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:04.880 --> 00:25:09.200
like Amanda, he too was corrupt, and strayed&nbsp;
from the original teachings of John Kramer.

00:25:09.200 --> 00:25:12.320
However, as one of the last men&nbsp;
standing, he had too much power,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:12.320 --> 00:25:14.960
and was nearly unstoppable&nbsp;
within a matter of weeks.

00:25:14.960 --> 00:25:17.680
Amanda actually may have played&nbsp;
a key role in helping to stop&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:17.680 --> 00:25:21.040
him though. By telling Corbett Denlon&nbsp;
not to trust the man who rescues her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:21.040 --> 00:25:24.000
she was able to get the message&nbsp;
out about Hoffman indirectly.

00:25:24.000 --> 00:25:27.280
This is never confirmed in the movies,&nbsp;
but we can assume that after Hoffman&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:27.280 --> 00:25:30.560
rescued Corbett after the conclusion of&nbsp;
the events at the meat packing plant,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:30.560 --> 00:25:34.800
that Corbett went on to tell the FBI that&nbsp;
someone warned her not to trust her rescuer.

00:25:34.800 --> 00:25:39.920
So this could be the reason that the FBI refuses&nbsp;
to stop investigating him even after his name is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:39.920 --> 00:25:43.120
cleared, the reason that he eventually&nbsp;
gets caught and has to go on the run,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:43.120 --> 00:25:48.320
which EVENTUALLY leads to his downfall. None of&nbsp;
it may have happened if not for Amanda Young.

00:25:48.320 --> 00:25:50.320
I’m still not going to call&nbsp;
her a hero or anything,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:50.320 --> 00:25:53.680
but throughout most of her story there&nbsp;
are multiple factors at play in her head,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:53.680 --> 00:25:57.680
so hopefully this video helped you understand her&nbsp;
mindset and some of the choices that she made.

00:25:57.680 --> 00:26:01.120
